1 NAME Peter Benjamin /Wildey/
2 GIVN Peter Benjamin
2 SURN Wildey
2 _MARNM Wildey
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 OCT 1913
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 DEC 2013
2 ADDR
3 CITY Alexandra
3 STAE Otago
3 CTRY New Zealand
1 OCCU Mining Engineer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Go hear to listen to a radio interview with Peter Wildey reflecting on his time as a young lieutenant in the 2nd world war.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://nzhistory.govt.nz/media/sound/interview-peter-wildey-part-1
2 CONT
2 CONT More war recounts here https://www.odt.co.nz/lifestyle/magazine/sapper-recalls-exploits-front
2 CONT
2 CONT  Later years he lived in Alexandra, Otago and that is where he died aged 100. His sister Caren also made a good age and died at 101 in Dunedin, Otago.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the war he married army nurse Mary Crawford in Cairo, Egypt, which meant the end of service for Mrs Wildey - a senior staff member had noticed her wedding ring, which was not allowed while on duty, but she would not take it
2 CONC  off and gladly returned home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Wildey followed soon afterwards.
2 CONT
2 CONT They settled in Maori Hill, Dunedin, created a large vegetable garden and chicken coop, and raised three daughters - Ms James, Gillian Heatherington and Ms Wildey. Peter was a civil engineer for the Otago Harbour Board.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following detail from this article Oct 2013 https://www.odt.co.nz/regions/central-otago/centenarian-believes-longevity-genes
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Wildey moved to Alexandra 23 years ago after his wife died. He  live in his own house un til his death..
2 CONT
2 CONT He said his favourite things about Alexandra were the summer heat and trout fishing. He was also a keen bowler and singer in the RSA Gentlemen's Choir until recently.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ms Wildey (Alison) said her father had a quadruple bypass 15 years ago and had led a fulfilling life since, but was now suffering from congestive heart failure. However, he still loved to read.
2 CONT
2 CONT So, what is the secret to a long life?
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Wildey reckons it is in a person's genes - his older sister Caren died just before her 102nd birthday, his cousin Les Lyders is still milking cows at 103 and his uncle Ben Lyders, who had smoked since he was 12, died aged 98.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Wildey will celebrate his birthday tomorrow at a lunch with 30 family members, including five grandchildren and six great-grandchildren who have arrived from around the country, and later at an afternoon tea with friends.
