2 CONT https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/data/batches/whi_doxy_ver01/data/sn85040451/00414214629/1920012101/0443.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT DANIEL BIRKELO TAKES OWN
2 CONT LIFE BY HANGING
2 CONT Failing Eyesight and the Horror of
2 CONT Approaching Blindness Is Reason
2 CONT the Rash Act
2 CONT The community was startled Saturday afternoon to learn that Daniel
2 CONT Birkelo, who resides with his son in
2 CONT the north-west part of the city, had
2 CONT committed suicled. He had been
2 CONT deeply despondent for some time over
2 CONT failing eyesight, being almost totally blind, with no hope of improvement.
2 CONT At 11:30 in the afternoon he went up- stairs, and a few minutes later his
2 CONT wife was horrified to find his lifeless body dangling from the bed post.
2 CONT Mr. Birkelo was a Christian man,
2 CONT qt one time member of the Lutheran
2 CONT church, who raised his family in an
2 CONT exemplary manner and enjoyed the
2 CONT respect of all who knew him. That
2 CONT his physical affliction so preyed upon
2 CONT his mind as to unbalance him mentally, no one will question, and only sympathy and not censurp is express- ed concerning his action.
2 CONT Mr. Birkelo was born in Norway in
2 CONT 1859. He came to New York in 1877,
2 CONT living subsequently in Crawford county, Minnesota, South Dakota, and Viroqua. He was married at I.aCrosse
2 CONT in 1887 to Martina Anderson of Bristow. Four children were born to this
2 CONT union: Mrs. W. J. Schellhas of Winona, Minnesota; Mrs. Albert Sheer
2 CONT of Richland Center, Mrs. Ernest Pierce and Peter Birkelo of Viroqua. One
2 CONT brother out of the family of nine children Fives at Ferryville. Funeral services were conducted by Rev. Raml>erg at the Main st.-eet church Tuesday afternoon. Extreme condolence
2 CONT is extended to the aged widow and children in their sorrow
